From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bernardo Pereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 16:31:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] assignment: move the left-hand side into the target instead
 of cloning

The assignment parser converted its left-hand side with the borrowing
AssignTarget conversions, which clone a property access, then dropped the
original. Cloning and dropping those chains was about 13% of the parse
samples for reCAPTCHA's recaptcha__en.js, redis.io's securemetrics script
and qualified.js.

The owned conversions move it instead. Parse time for nine third-party
scripts (3.0 MiB): 296 -> 278 ms natively. ASTs, collected source text,
errors and top-level bytecode for 6009 npm files are unchanged.
---
 src/parser/expression/assignment/mod.rs | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/parser/expression/assignment/mod.rs b/src/parser/expression/assignment/mod.rs
index 31260fd..aae98ed 100644
--- a/src/parser/expression/assignment/mod.rs
+++ b/src/parser/expression/assignment/mod.rs
@@ -291,7 +291,8 @@ impl AssignmentExpression {
                         None
                     };

-                    if let Some(target) = AssignTarget::from_expression(&lhs, cursor.strict()) {
+                    if let Some(target) = AssignTarget::from_expression_owned(lhs, cursor.strict())
+                    {
                         return Ok(AssignmentStep::Target((target, AssignOp::Assign, lhs_name)));
                     }
                     return Err(Error::lex(LexError::Syntax(
@@ -302,7 +303,7 @@ impl AssignmentExpression {
                 TokenKind::Punctuator(p) if p.as_assign_op().is_some() => {
                     cursor.advance(interner);
                     if let Some(target) =
-                        AssignTarget::from_expression_simple(&lhs, cursor.strict())
+                        AssignTarget::from_expression_simple_owned(lhs, cursor.strict())
                     {
                         let assignop = p.as_assign_op().expect("assignop disappeared");
                         let name = if (assignop == AssignOp::BoolAnd
